                <pb facs="0409" n="315" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg315"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/3139: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the President’s Personal Representative in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-05-01T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1, 1924—2
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>12. Your 14, April 28, 2 p.m. Department approves of steps taken by you and of
                    the policy indicated. You are authorized to state that this Government will lend
                    its moral support to the Provisional Government of General Tosta constituted in
                    accordance with the agreement quoted in your telegram. The Department takes this
                    opportunity to commend you for bringing about a satisfactory solution of the
                    Honduran difficulties.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
